  "faq": {
    "title": "Frequently Asked Questions",
    "q1": "1. What is Wheel Match?",
    "a1": "Wheel Match is a platform that connects patients and vendors to help find the most suitable wheelchair based on individual needs and preferences.",
    "q2": "2. How do I get started?",
    "a2": "Simply click on Sign Up from the homepage and choose your role (Patient or Vendor) to begin the onboarding process.",
    "q3": "3. Is the platform free to use?",
    "a3": "Yes! Creating an account and getting matched with a wheelchair recommendation is completely free. Some services or vendor offerings may have costs.",
    "q4": "4. Can I edit my personal or medical info later?",
    "a4": "Yes. After signing in, you can go to your profile to update personal information, medical history, or preferences at any time.",
    "q5": "5. How are wheelchair recommendations made?",
    "a5": "Our system ranks wheelchairs from your medical profile (morphology, pathology, propulsion type) against vendor inventory, with clear reasons for each suggestion.",
    "q6": "6. Who approves wheelchair requests?",
    "a6": "There is no approval step. Your choice from the AI-ranked recommendations is final — confirm it in My wheelchairs and contact the vendor for fulfillment.",
    "q7": "7. What do vendors do on the platform?",
    "a7": "Vendors receive qualified leads, offer personalized wheelchair options, and can schedule fittings or test sessions with patients.",
    "q8": "8. How can I contact support?",
    "contactLead": "You can email us at",
    "contactAnd": "or call us at",
    "contactEnd": "We're happy to help!"
  },
